ACAD_STRLSORT: catalogue sorting must not depend on MAXSORT
Status: DONE
Resolved: 2026-10-16, clautolisp/alfe 2.3.23, specification 0.14.4

Dialect classification: case 0, shared AutoCAD/BricsCAD behavior.
The SCHMS catalogue contains 204 entries. The BricsCAD default MAXSORT=200
caused the runtime to return nil instead of sorting this list. That gate
was based on an incorrect specification assumption.

Native AutoCAD 2022 and BricsCAD V25 both sorted 204 strings with MAXSORT
set to 0, 1, 2, 200 and 1000. MAXSORT controls named GUI lists, not this
function. Removed the artificial gate and the false AutoCAD-only warning.
Regression coverage exercises 204 and 1001 strings, including MAXSORT=0.
The reusable observation probe is probe-acad-strlsort-maxsort.lsp.

Factory defaults remain dialect-dependent: 200 for BricsCAD and 1000 for
AutoCAD, clautolisp and lax. Tests pin these defaults and preserve explicit
user values across dialect changes. Users of GUI sorting should choose a
MAXSORT value appropriate to their data, within 0..32767.
Exact non-ASCII collation and memory-failure parity remain separately
tracked in deferred-spec-research.issue.

Sources:
https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2025/ENG/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-7AD30968-4982-4E1C-9847-69A5EAEB7C63.htm
https://developer.bricsys.com/bricscad/help/en_US/V22/DevRef/source/acad_strlsort.htm
